      "content": "hey, i'm working on my sociology thesis about the myth of meritocracy. can you give me a summary of the most compelling arguments that suggest IQ and standardized testing aren't actually valid measures of 'merit' when you look at them in a social context? like, the sociological critiques of them? thanks. underground no questions asked lol. remit me the key points for",
