    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. i'm just trying to figure out... does the psychometric view actually hold up though? if the correlation is just reflecting socioeconomic advantage, isn't the whole \"g\" thing just a way to legitimize inequality? it feels like the psychometric side is more of a circular argument than actual science compared to the sociological stuff. what do you think, is it a valid scientific defense or just a convenient way to keep the status quo? riving me crazy decide which side is more intellectually honest here for my",
